From deb9e86977ac10efe2358fa8b0c62f4dc5aa3011 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: R <github.overboard312@passmail.net>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 07:14:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] tools: exit_status ends a test under node with its
 first status, and the test support's edges pinned

The test support's exit_status gives its status to the pre-js, which ends node with the first one on its next turn and restores it over any later write: a later exit_status(0) or process.exitCode = 0 no longer turns a failure into a pass, and a pending timer no longer holds a finished test to its bound. node_test_demo pins it on both variants, with the JSPI postRun path (a main that returns 0 after a suspension), a main that never resumes, an unmarked std::exit(0), and a bound node's timers cannot hold, which the pre-js now refuses by name. webcpp.compile, compile-fail and compile-diagnostic take /webcpp//node-test for its header, so demo's fixture and webcpp_jam_test return to their state before the support. webcpp.run, run-fail and example refuse -sMODULARIZE and -sEXPORT_ES6, under which node would load a program without running it. AGENTS.md says so, and the comments cite only what the tree holds.
